  "articleBody": "It can be frustrating when your local business isn't getting the AI visibility you expect. You've got great services, but AI Overviews, Siri, or Alexa just aren't recommending you. Often, the issue isn't your service quality, but how your online presence is structured for machine consumption. AI systems thrive on clarity, direct answers, and structured data, and if your site isn't optimized for these, you're likely missing out on being cited.\n\nWhat to Do Next\n\n1. Review your content for direct answers: Go through your key service pages. Can you find clear, concise answers to common questions about your services within the first few sentences? AI systems love this. If answers are buried or vague, revise them to be more direct and factual, including specifics like qualifications, locations, or dates where relevant.\n\n2. Check for hidden or inaccessible information: Make sure important details about your services, pricing, or hours aren't locked away in images, PDFs, or complex JavaScript elements. AI crawlers struggle with these formats, preferring plain, visible text. Ensure your contact info and service descriptions are easily readable by bots.\n\n3. Verify your business information consistency: Search for your business across various platforms – Google Business Profile, Yelp, your own website. Is your name, address, phone number, and service list identical everywhere? Inconsistencies can confuse AI systems and reduce their confidence in recommending you.\n\n4. Explore structured data opportunities: While not a magic bullet, using schema markup (like `LocalBusiness`, `Service`, or `FAQPage`) can help AI understand your content better. Ensure any existing schema is valid and accurately reflects your page content, following feature-specific guidelines. Don't add schema for things not explicitly on the page.\n\n5. Consider a professional AI visibility audit: If you've tried these steps and are still struggling, especially with a large or complex site, it might be time to bring in an expert. A qualified professional can perform a technical audit, analyze crawl errors, and distinguish real technical issues from speculative AI ranking claims, ensuring your efforts are focused and effective.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
